# An anonymous `{ k }` destructure of a map with neither a `"k"` nor a `:k`
# key is a pattern mismatch at the `let`, on both backends. The walker used
# to leave `k` unbound and fail later with "Undefined variable", while BEAM
# raised an Erlang badkey.
main do
  let { port } = { host: "localhost" }
  IO.printLine(port)
end
